## The key decision

For your TFT-heavy Arduino projects, **full ESP32 QEMU alone will frustrate you** because display/peripheral emulation is the hard part.

The strongest product is:

```text
QEMU for real ESP32 firmware execution
+
native Arduino shim for beautiful TFT simulation
+
optional bridge between them later
```

That gives you something useful quickly, while still leaving room for “real fake ESP32 board” mode later.

